course: dictionary
lesson: 8943
title: Silicon, the stuff in sand and chips
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Silicon is a chemical element, shown by the symbol Si. It is a grey, shiny solid, and it is the main part of sand and many rocks. «Light hits thin slices of silicon and knocks tiny electrons loose» tells you that silicon is a material that can make electricity from light.
explain: Silicon is a noun, but it is uncountable, like water or sand. You say some silicon, not a silicon. Context helps you work out what it is: «A computer chip has billions of tiny switches printed layer by layer with light onto very pure silicon» shows that silicon is the material a chip is made on.
explain: Read the words around silicon to find its job. «Inside your phone is a computer chip smaller than a fingernail, printed onto a thin slice of silicon» tells you that silicon is the base for the chip. Then swap in your meaning: a chip printed onto some grey, shiny material still makes sense.
fact: Silicon is a chemical element with the symbol Si.
fact: Silicon is a grey, shiny solid found in sand and many rocks.
fact: Silicon is used to make computer chips and solar panels.
fact: Silicon is uncountable, so say some silicon, not a silicon.
fact: Silicon Valley in California is a famous area for tech companies.
exercise: In «Light hits thin slices of silicon and knocks tiny electrons loose», what is the silicon? | A kind of light | A tiny switch | *The material the slices are made of | Dust from the sky
exercise: What is silicon mainly found in? | *Sand and many rocks | Clouds | Wood | Water
exercise: Silicon is uncountable. Which phrase is right? | a silicon | many silicons | *some silicon | silicons
test: What is the chemical symbol for silicon? | Sn | Sl | S | *Si
test: Which material is used to make computer chips? | *Silicon | Wood | Paper | Sand only
exam: According to «Inside your phone is a computer chip smaller than a fingernail, printed onto a thin slice of silicon», what is the chip printed onto? | A tiny battery | *A thin slice of silicon | Glass | A metal wire
